      "writtenOn": "2023-07-28T20:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think partners rely on the fact that COMMON_GKI_MODULES_LIST is the aarch64 GKI list.\n\nPerhaps we should actively break it by deleting `COMMON_GKI_MODULES_LIST` variable completely? Of course, announce it in GKI newsletter first.\n\n---\n\nAlso, there\u0027s no good way to \"deprecate\" variables in Bazel, but functions can be deprecated properly (by adding the \"Deprecated:\" section in doc). Perhaps this should be a function instead? e.g. `get_gki_modules_list(\"arm64\")`\n\nThis way if we need to deprecate more things in the future, we have more control.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "11646b716e1c3b749790e081868d28df450b8081",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
